"><br /> Then why don't you go on those forums and post about it there?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm mildly curious which forums you think conversation about a system introduced in a Chronicles crossover supplement properly belongs in. You doing okay there, Shad?<br /> <br /> Anyways, on the larger topic at hand, it's definitely a pretty cool dramatic system, but admittedly I haven't been able to personally try it out yet. Anyone have any experience giving it a go?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-28-2024, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T10:55:47-07:00","id":1539431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1539389-agonism?p=1539429#post1539429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I didn't paid much attention to those systems, although I may reread Contagion soon, so I'll keep an eye on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Agonism is worth picking out of Contagion Chronicle even if CC is not what you're doing. Tastes vary; you may not want the Chronicles to be any less Dark. I want them to be a <i>tiny bit</i> less dark. To have just a hint that victory is <i>possible</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T11:02:37-07:00","id":1539433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1539389-agonism?p=1539430#post1539430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm mildly curious which forums you think conversation about a system introduced in a Chronicles crossover supplement properly belongs in. You doing okay there, Shad?<br /> <br /> Anyways, on the larger topic at hand, it's definitely a pretty cool dramatic system, but admittedly I haven't been able to personally try it out yet. Anyone have any experience giving it a go?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume general Chronicles. If you can correct me about that, please do. By the way, I didn't apologize to you about the old demon business because I thought the truer courtesy would be to <i>not </i>ping your notifications again.<br /> <br /> Right, sorry, that wasn't for me. I stand by the content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":". 07-28-2024, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T11:27:42-07:00","id":1539435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1539389-agonism?p=1539433#post1539433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume general Chronicles. If you can correct me about that, please do. By the way, I didn't apologize to you about the old demon business because I thought the truer courtesy would be to <i>not </i>ping your notifications again.<br /> <br /> Right, sorry, that wasn't for me. I stand by the content.</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps to stay on topic. So, back to the question, got any experiences with using Agonism in a game yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T12:06:32-07:00","id":1539437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1539389-agonism?p=1539435#post1539435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It helps to stay on topic. So, back to the question, got any experiences with using Agonism in a game yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only just started using it, but already the players are angling to be more supportive of others' Aspirations and build up those Trusting Conditions. These are people who would do a fair amount for one another in real life, but not so much at the table.<br /> <br /> I don't think this is mentioned in any of the books that have this system, but it's a great Storyteller tool. It mechanically approximately tracks spotlight time, and my (short) experience is that you can hook everyone by hooking the one who has the most Social Currency at the moment. No one feels like they're betraying their character concept by pausing on an Aspiration.<br /> <br /> I guess it's just that &quot;personal satisfaction&quot; and &quot;because we're friends&quot; carry less weight in an imaginary world where everything <i>but </i>those is a magic bean on your character sheet. Other groups may not work this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":".  Thought of more 07-28-2024, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T15:52:58-07:00","id":1539504,"title":"","content":"I remember seeing the system in <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i>, it seems like a great mechanical incentive to build character synergy, as well as facilitate giving equal time and investment to each party member.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T15:56:59-07:00","id":1539505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1539389-agonism?p=1539504#post1539504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember seeing the system in <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i>, it seems like a great mechanical incentive to build character synergy, as well as facilitate giving equal time and investment to each party member.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I missed it there. I didn't read Tome of the Pentacle right through. I probably should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T17:35:33-07:00","id":1539509,"title":"","content":"Looked at it. Cabal Friction has a few new wrinkles. Probably worth porting back to Agonism if you use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T10:09:09-07:00","id":1539533,"title":"","content":"The thing in Cabal Friction about taking Guilty or Shaken at negative Social Currency is interesting, although I'm not really feeling Shaken. Stoic would be better, if you use Stoic. In fact, I think I prefer Stoic to Shaken for all interactions with Agonism and variants. I don't see why capitulation would resolve Shaken.<br /> <br /> It might make sense to apply Guilty or Stoic at zero, rather than only at negative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T14:18:13-07:00","id":1539559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1539389-agonism?p=1539533#post1539533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing in Cabal Friction about taking Guilty or Shaken at negative Social Currency is interesting, although I'm not really feeling Shaken. Stoic would be better, if you use Stoic. In fact, I think I prefer Stoic to Shaken for all interactions with Agonism and variants. I don't see why capitulation would resolve Shaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main sources of negative social currency in the Cabal Friction iteration of the system is from pursuing your Obsessions with the aid/at the expense of others and not making good on it before the beginning of the next chapter. Stoic is certainly a choice, but it's not one that really gels with a splat whose magic spills out of them more when they do stuff equivalent to what gives Sleepers the Guilty and Shaken Conditions and whose natural equivalents to those conditions are about being <i>less</i> reserved with regards to revealing their true feelings.<br /> <br /> Capitulation resolves Shaken in the same fashion as it resolves Guilty \u2014 you're letting your cabalmate have their way and hoping that eases off any hard feelings from you getting to pursue your Obsessions on their dime, and in turn that may further lead them to accord you some of the staked social currency as one of the losing parties in the negotiation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It might make sense to apply Guilty or Stoic at zero, rather than only at negative. </div> </div> </div>That would be nonsensical, not least because Social Currency moves towards zero at the end of every chapter and the Stoic Condition adds another block to any attempts to raise Wisdom (in addition to referencing a Condition that isn't printed in Mage 2e Core nor Tome of the Pentacle).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T15:45:37-07:00","id":1539560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1539389-agonism?p=1539559#post1539559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be nonsensical, not least because Social Currency moves towards zero at the end of every chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, that's an excellent point.<br /> <br /> For the rest, what I meant, though admittedly did not say, was that <i>if </i>you were porting the &quot;take a Condition for negative Social Currency&quot; part of Cabal Friction to other variants, Stoic would be better than Shaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":".  Chopped quote to make it clear to what I was responding 07-30-2024, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}